      "writtenOn": "2023-02-24T22:17:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`frameIndex`. This is the frame we want to decode.\n\nI wish we could just pass it as part of the `Options` object, but I don\u0027t think that\u0027s possible. We need to copy the existing `Options` object, but we also need to copy the `SkAndroidCodec::Options` portion of it, and `SkCodec` can\u0027t do that without knowing about `SkAndroidCodec`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 946,
        "startChar": 71,
        "endLine": 946,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "fefbe4ab4a24db99ead03e54ec819ad6ec681699",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2165a28a_1fbb48c7",
        "filename": "include/codec/SkCodec.h",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 946,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-27T13:39:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. That was what my experimentation led to as well. If we pass in a \n`const SkAndroidCodec::AndroidOptions\u0026` as a `const SkCodec::Options\u0026`, we can \"unpack\" it again using reinterpret_cast without losing the data however, we cannot modify or copy the contents. Thus, we have to pass the frame index separately to something that knows how to copy an `SkAndroidCodec::AndroidOptions`.\n\nAdded comment to explain that.",
      "parentUuid": "d1b59d9b_9a3bdf5a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 946,
        "startChar": 71,
        "endLine": 946,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "fefbe4ab4a24db99ead03e54ec819ad6ec681699",
